# DS Tripwire fleet DENY list - md5s of files identified as malware, one per line, with a NAME.
# Fetched hourly by every site. A hash committed here NAMES the finding in the alert within one cron
# cycle ("KNOWN MALWARE: <name>"), which is what matters when someone is triaging twenty alerts at 3am.
#
# SAFETY: a deny entry only labels a finding the behaviour engine has ALREADY scored. It never creates
# a finding, so a wrong hash here costs a wrong label on a real finding and can never manufacture an
# alert on a clean file. Only list hashes of files you have read.
#
# Format: <32 hex>  <name shown in the alert>
